 reported itself complete. That is exactly how insertion codes hid in the StructQC panel. Each feature is witnessed from the evidence an executed case produced, and execution fails if any required feature has no witness.","required_features":["curated_residue_resolved","curated_residue_unresolved","metal_ligand_role","declared_cofactor_observed","declared_cofactor_absent","declared_cofactor_unmappable","missing_evidence_reported"],"unwitnessable_features":{"curated_residue_missing_coordinates":{"declared_by":"the panel's coverage_rules, as incomplete controls","resolution":"Curate a structure with a disordered catalytic residue.","status":"NOT SATISFIED - recorded rather than claimed","why_not_witnessed":"1ALG's curated residues fall outside the modelled fragment entirely, so site-context reports unresolved_mapping. missing_coordinates needs a residue inside the reference map but disordered in the coordinates."},"curated_residue_substituted":{"declared_by":"the panel's coverage_rules, as modified controls","resolution":"Curate a substituted structure of a protein not otherwise in the panel.","status":"NOT SATISFIED - recorded rather than claimed","why_not_witnessed":"A role_mismatch needs a structure whose curated residue is substituted. The four found (1FQG E164N, 4ZNB C181S, 2NQ9 Y72A, 4K1G H69A) are each alternative structures of proteins already used in other strata, so adopting one would put a single homolog group in two strata."}}},"functional_site":{"cofactor_declaration_source":"UniProt COFACTOR annotation, joined to PDB component ids through an explicit ChEBI table. Declaring from UniProt rather than from the coordinate file is what makes the gate non-vacuous: a cofactor the structure lacks is still declared and reported not_observed.","cofactor_identifier_match":"exact","component_map_note":"Every case supplies the ChEBI-to-component map, not only the metal stratum. Without it a declared cofactor resolves to \"unresolved\" rather than \"not_observed\", which would let an apo or fragment structure look merely unmapped instead of missing its cofactor.","false_exact_mappings_max":0,"missing_state_accuracy":"exact","note":"The recovery floor is written for complete structures. The apo/modified/incomplete stratum exists to carry structures whose curated residues cannot all be resolved -- 1ALG resolves none of five -- so applying the floor there would fail the stratum for doing its job. Those cases are held to their declared per-site states instead, which is the stricter test.","recovery_floor_exempt_strata":["apo_modified_or_incomplete"],"unambiguous_curated_residue_recovery_min":0.95},"missing_evidence_behavior":{"expected_missing_by_stratum":{"acid_base":["pocket_results"],"apo_modified_or_incomplete":["pocket_results"],"metal_or_cofactor":["pocket_results"],"nucleophile_or_covalent":["pocket_results"]},"mode":"fail_closed","rule":"No pocket predictor is run, so every case reports pocket_results missing. Declared per stratum so the absence is stated, not tolerated."}},"runtime":{"machine":"x86_64","platform":"Darwin","python":"3.12.7"},"schema_version":"1.0","scientific_execution_performed":true,"scope_qualification_note":"Passing execution is not scope qualification. A Mark 1 scope is qualified only when its panel composes, every case and control passes, and the result reproduces independently on a second machine. This runner reports execution only; it never sets a qualification gate, and scope_qualified is always false here by construction.","scope_qualified":false,"strata_executed":["acid_base","apo_modified_or_incomplete","metal_or_cofactor","nucleophile_or_covalent"],"stratum":null,"stratum_state":"passed"}
